Correction to my earlier comment on this PR: it said `img2 install` was **not** run. It has now been run — in a throwaway `$IMG2_HOME` under a temp directory, touching nothing of an existing setup — and it changed the page, which is the point.

What it showed:

- three steps: create the home (`plugins/`, `generated/`, `backups/`, `plugins.json {"version":1,"plugins":[]}`, `receipts.json []`) → clone the harness into `$IMG2_HOME/harness` → configure agent access;
- the clone follows the repository's **default branch, not the newest tag** (measured `v0.4.0-1-g06634bd`);
- with **no writable directory on `PATH`** it links no launcher at all: it warns `No writable launcher directory on PATH; use npx instead` and prints the `npx` form — which is why the command block is written to work with or without a launcher;
- host settings are touched only for a host it actually detects (`Claude Code not detected; settings left unchanged`).

The page now also leads with the part a brand-new user hits first, which my first draft got backwards: **every command works before you install anything**, as `npx --yes @img2threejs/img2@latest <command>` — measured on an empty home, `--version --json` and `list` exit 0 and write no file (`list` reports `Registered 0`), `capabilities` answers `providers: []`, and only `doctor` exits 1, saying `no harness checkout at <home>; run img2 install`. A `generic` or `character` run needs no harness and no plugins at all; the harness exists for when a domain plugin serves the item.

Two process notes on this PR, since they are visible in its history: the page asserted the install command from the upstream README before anything had been run, and correcting it took several rewrites of the branch. Both are on me; the content is now measured rather than read, and further corrections will be new commits rather than rewrites.
